& [AuthorityAudit]
  + the user target authorizes source-to-substrate planning and SJS contract formation
  + it expressly withholds workspace mutation process launch commit push self-signature provider installation persistence remote FPGA and Minecraft effects
  + the historical Phase3B signature is valid for formation only and lists renewed satisfaction signature plus target-host proof as activation prerequisites
  + the historical Phase3C signature is valid for formation only and lists inventory quiescence publication reconstruction test review and later handoff prerequisites
  + no current artifact grants a live writer, evidence-root writer, rollback executor, cleanup executor, commit broker, push broker, or SOP activation capability
  + therefore full SWPB formation is authorized while implementation and physical activation remain absent

& [PredecessorSemantics]
  + SWA-03 supplies a bounded replay-valid lifecycle step and attempt identity without capability issuance
  + SWA-04A supplies a strict complete representation-only update proposal and self-consistent prior admission forms without freshness authentication or physical observation
  + Phase3A supplies current read-only workspace admission semantics but any saved receipt remains nonfresh
  + the current live Codex adapter proves a read-only no-network one-turn transport only; its readOnly sandbox cannot be widened transitively to workspaceWrite
  + Phase3B and Phase3C supply design vocabulary and threat knowledge but no implementation authority

& [RequiredCorrectionsToHistoricalFormation]
  + bind the current SWA-03 and SWA-04A causal lineage rather than only a generic Phase3A receipt
  + separate B0 through B5 commissions so pure protocol code cannot instantiate physical authority
  + treat exact current executable protocol schema and environment identity as activation inputs rather than stable historical facts
  + make authenticated receipt provenance explicit because structural receipt equality is insufficient
  + distinguish evidence-root writes from candidate writes and both from rollback and cleanup authority
  + bind proposed-versus-observed reconciliation explicitly rather than permitting a writer report or notification diff to define post-state
  + retain rollback attempt incomplete and quarantine dispositions without claiming automatic restoration
  + keep commit push succeeding-SOP authorship signature and activation entirely downstream

& [DataClasses]
  + strict decoded metadata plans carry only bounded identities digests paths policies resources capabilities stages and commissions
  + physical handles process owners current filesystem carriers evidence-root carriers reviewer contexts and rollback capabilities remain separately constructed under their own activation source
  + outputs carry lineage-retaining receipts with exact stage disposition consequence account and unresolved frontier
  + every self-digest excludes only its own field and uses deterministic closed serialization
  + no output receipt is deserializable into an authority-bearing runtime handle

& [ClosedValidationOrder]
  + profile and generation
  + complete predecessor and self-digest integrity
  + lifecycle step attempt and proposal correspondence
  + capability account and stage commission
  + single-use and replay identities
  + current-interface and host bindings when physically activated
  + path root repository policy and budget bounds
  + event process terminal and consequence accounting
  + direct post-state evidence and proposed-versus-observed reconciliation
  + deterministic acceptance gates
  + rollback reobservation or quarantine disposition
  + nonauthority and downstream stop rules

& [ThreatLedger]
  + [T01] stale self-consistent admission launders freshness
  + [T02] pure proposal or digest launders write authority
  + [T03] historical formation signature launders implementation authority
  + [T04] read-only adapter semantics are widened to workspaceWrite
  + [T05] executable version or protocol drift is ignored
  + [T06] writable-root path alias link reparse hard-link stream mount temp or Git common-directory escape
  + [T07] notification or model report launders preventive or post-state truth
  + [T08] event budget is checked only after unbounded retention
  + [T09] child descendant late writer or incomplete interruption is missed
  + [T10] writer self-verifies or self-accepts mutable state
  + [T11] evidence-root capability overlaps candidate mutation capability
  + [T12] unexpected untracked ignored index ref principal or outside-policy state is omitted
  + [T13] accepted evidence launders commit push deployment activation or current-world truth
  + [T14] rollback request launders successful restoration or cleanup
  + [T15] retry overwrites evidence or reuses single-use authority
  + [T16] provider or generated SOP widens mutation authority
  + [T17] synthetic fixture is reported as live physical work
  + [T18] foreign draft source is imported into the active authority chain

